      <title>Squeak 2.27.5</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:34:44 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22705</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.27.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>A queued message has its own Steer button on its line: one click sends it into the running turn. Clicking the line still opens the whole message to edit or remove it.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.27.4</h4><ul><li>The chat no longer jumps, flickers or shows a message twice while it updates. Every message has exactly one row from the moment you press Send: a message you send while Claude works is its queued line at once (no card above the composer that later moves into the chat), a steer is a dimmed row at the end of the running turn that turns solid in the same place when the agent reads it, and the reply being written is the running turn's last row, the place the finished reply takes. A randomized test races the host's events, the queue and your presses in 600 orders and fails on any duplicate, reordered, vanished or reappearing row.</li><li>A queued message is one short line in the chat (its first words, how many pictures, "Queued"). Click it to see the whole message and Steer, Edit or Remove it. Editing changes the words and keeps the pictures.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.27.3</h4><ul><li>A message you steer into a working chat shows once: dimmed at the bottom until the agent takes it in, then in its place. It no longer also showed solid at the same time.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
